  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Toruro. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Toruro is a Spanish trick-taking gambling game for 5+ players using a 40-card Spanish deck. There are three pots (Cabeza, Barriga, Cola), one for each trick. Players decide whether to 'go' (ir) or pass, and those who go must win at least one trick or pay a penalty (Lulo). The card ranking features the unusual A-3-K order common in L'Hombre games.",
    objective: 'Win tricks to claim the three pots (Cabeza, Barriga, Cola); players who go must win at least one trick or pay a lulo penalty.',
    gameplay: '1. Deal 3 cards + 1 trump indicator. 2. Declare: Ir (go) or pass. Must win 1+ trick if going. 3. Exchange cards (0-3). If exchanging 3, get 4 and keep best 3. 4. Play 3 tricks. Follow suit. Must trump if void. 5. First trick: Must lead Ace of trumps if held. 6. Second trick: Must lead highest trump.',
